## No Information Rate: 0.5107 | P-Value [Acc &gt; NIR]: &lt; 2.22e-16</code></pre>
<div id="attitudes-summary-plot" class="section level3">
<h3>Attitudes Summary Plot</h3>
<p>The attitudes track has shown a significant increase in predictive
accuracy, rising from about 68% in the 1980s to 86% in the 2020s—an 18
percentage point improvement. In comparison, the demographics track only
improved by about 7 percentage points. This suggests that ideological
beliefs, rather than demographic factors, are the main drivers of
partisan sorting. Both logistic regression and random forest models show
similar trends, confirming the robustness of these findings.</p>
<p>This aligns with research by <span class="citation">Murphy and
Zhirnov (2020)</span>, which noted increasing issue partisanship from
1972 to 2016, and <span class="citation">Ojer et al. (2025)</span>, who
found that different demographic groups are diverging ideologically. The
accuracy of 86% in the 2020s greatly surpasses the 64% limit found in
demographics-only models by <span class="citation">Kim and Zilinsky
(2022)</span>, reinforcing the idea that attitudes are what shape modern
partisan identity.</p>
<pre class="r"><code>all_att &lt;- rbind(logreg_results_att, rf_results_att)
all_att$decade &lt;- factor(all_att$decade, levels = decades)

att_colors &lt;- c(&quot;Logistic Regression&quot; = &quot;#7b68ee&quot;, &quot;Random Forest&quot; = &quot;#2d8659&quot;)

ggplot(all_att, aes(x = decade, y = accuracy, color = model, group = model)) +
  geom_line(linewidth = 1.2) +
  geom_point(size = 3) +
  geom_text(aes(label = paste0(accuracy, &quot;%&quot;)), vjust = -1, size = 3) +
  scale_color_manual(values = att_colors) +
  scale_y_continuous(limits = c(55, 95), labels = function(x) paste0(x, &quot;%&quot;)) +
  geom_hline(yintercept = 50, linetype = &quot;dashed&quot;, color = &quot;gray50&quot;, alpha = 0.5) +
  labs(title = &quot;Attitudes-Only Models: Accuracy by Decade (MICE Imputation)&quot;,
       subtitle = &quot;67% → 86% accuracy | Strong support for H1: ideological sorting increasing&quot;,
       x = &quot;&quot;, y = &quot;Test Accuracy&quot;, color = &quot;Model&quot;) +
  theme_party</code></pre>
<pre><code>## Warning: Removed 1 row containing missing values or values outside the scale range
## (`geom_hline()`).</code></pre>
<p><img role="img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="672" /></p>
</div>
<div id="roc-curves-1980s-vs.-2020s" class="section level2">
<h2>ROC Curves: 1980s vs. 2020s</h2>
<div id="s" class="section level3">
<h3>1980s</h3>
<pre class="r"><code>roc_log_att  &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_att_80$party  == &quot;Republican&quot;), log_att_prob_80,  quiet = TRUE)
roc_rf_att   &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_att_80$party  == &quot;Republican&quot;), rf_att_prob_80,   quiet = TRUE)
roc_log_demo &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_demo_80$party == &quot;Republican&quot;), log_demo_prob_80, quiet = TRUE)
roc_rf_demo  &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_demo_80$party == &quot;Republican&quot;), rf_demo_prob_80,  quiet = TRUE)

plot(roc_log_att, col = &quot;#7b68ee&quot;, lwd = 2, 
     main = &quot;ROC Curves — 1980s Models&quot;)
lines(roc_rf_att, col = &quot;#2d8659&quot;, lwd = 2)
lines(roc_log_demo, col = &quot;#e6994a&quot;, lwd = 2)
lines(roc_rf_demo, col = &quot;#c9853a&quot;, lwd = 2, lty = 2)
abline(a = 0, b = 1, lty = 3, col = &quot;gray50&quot;)
legend(&quot;bottomright&quot;, 
       legend = c(
         paste0(&quot;Attitudes LogReg (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_log_att), 3), &quot;)&quot;),
         paste0(&quot;Attitudes RF (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_rf_att), 3), &quot;)&quot;),
         paste0(&quot;Demographics LogReg (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_log_demo), 3), &quot;)&quot;),
         paste0(&quot;Demographics RF (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_rf_demo), 3), &quot;)&quot;)
       ),
       col = c(&quot;#7b68ee&quot;, &quot;#2d8659&quot;, &quot;#e6994a&quot;, &quot;#c9853a&quot;),
       lwd = 2, lty = c(1, 1, 1, 2), cex = 0.9)</code></pre>
<p><img role="img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="672" /></p>
</div>
<div id="s-1" class="section level3">
<h3>2020s</h3>
<pre class="r"><code># ROC CURVES: 2020s
roc_log_att  &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_att_20$party  == &quot;Republican&quot;), log_att_prob_20,  quiet = TRUE)
roc_rf_att   &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_att_20$party  == &quot;Republican&quot;), rf_att_prob_20,   quiet = TRUE)
roc_log_demo &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_demo_20$party == &quot;Republican&quot;), log_demo_prob_20, quiet = TRUE)
roc_rf_demo  &lt;- roc(as.numeric(test_demo_20$party == &quot;Republican&quot;), rf_demo_prob_20,  quiet = TRUE)

plot(roc_log_att, col = &quot;#7b68ee&quot;, lwd = 2,
     main = &quot;ROC Curves — 2020s Models&quot;)
lines(roc_rf_att,   col = &quot;#2d8659&quot;, lwd = 2)
lines(roc_log_demo, col = &quot;#e6994a&quot;, lwd = 2)
lines(roc_rf_demo,  col = &quot;#c9853a&quot;, lwd = 2, lty = 2)
abline(a = 0, b = 1, lty = 3, col = &quot;gray50&quot;)
legend(&quot;bottomright&quot;,
       legend = c(paste0(&quot;Attitudes LogReg (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_log_att),  3), &quot;)&quot;),
                  paste0(&quot;Attitudes RF     (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_rf_att),   3), &quot;)&quot;),
                  paste0(&quot;Demographics LogReg (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_log_demo), 3), &quot;)&quot;),
                  paste0(&quot;Demographics RF  (AUC=&quot;, round(auc(roc_rf_demo),  3), &quot;)&quot;)),
       col = c(&quot;#7b68ee&quot;, &quot;#2d8659&quot;, &quot;#e6994a&quot;, &quot;#c9853a&quot;),
       lwd = 2, lty = c(1, 1, 1, 2), cex = 0.9)</code></pre>
<p><img role="img" src="data:image/png;base64," width="672" /></p>
<p>The two ROC panels show the main finding of the study. In the 1980s,
the performance of the attitude-based models and demographic models were
similar, with AUC values between 0.70 and 0.76. Neither was clearly
better. However, by the 2020s, the situation changed significantly. The
attitude-based curves (purple and green) improved to an AUC of about
0.93, while the demographic curves (orange) stayed around 0.77. The
small gap from the 1980s has turned into a significant difference in the
2020s. Although demographics like race, education, and income still have
some predictive power for party identification, attitudes about issues
such as abortion and government spending are now much more important.
Therefore, as was expected based on the reviewed literature,
demographics would not become more predictive over time; instead,
attitudes have become the main factor in American partisanship.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="grand-combined-plot" class="section level2">
<h2>Grand Combined Plot</h2>
<pre class="r"><code>grand &lt;- rbind(
  rf_results_att %&gt;% mutate(track = &quot;Attitudes (RF)&quot;) %&gt;% select(decade, track, accuracy),
  rf_results_demo %&gt;% mutate(track = &quot;Demographics (RF)&quot;) %&gt;% select(decade, track, accuracy)
)

grand$decade &lt;- factor(grand$decade, levels = c(&quot;1980s&quot;, &quot;1990s&quot;, &quot;2000s&quot;, &quot;2010s&quot;, &quot;2020s&quot;))

grand_colors &lt;- c(&quot;Attitudes (RF)&quot; = &quot;#2d8659&quot;,
                   &quot;Demographics (RF)&quot; = &quot;#c9853a&quot;)

ggplot(grand, aes(x = decade, y = accuracy, color = track, group = track)) +
  geom_line(linewidth = 1.2) +
  geom_point(size = 3) +
  geom_text(aes(label = paste0(accuracy, &quot;%&quot;)), vjust = -1, size = 3) +
  scale_color_manual(values = grand_colors) +
  scale_y_continuous(limits = c(55, 95), labels = function(x) paste0(x, &quot;%&quot;)) +
  geom_hline(yintercept = 50, linetype = &quot;dashed&quot;, color = &quot;gray50&quot;, alpha = 0.5) +
  labs(title = &quot;Model Accuracy Over Time: Demographics vs Attitudes&quot;,
       subtitle = &quot;Both tracks show increasing accuracy → H1 supported: ideological sorting is growing&quot;,
       x = &quot;&quot;, y = &quot;Test Accuracy&quot;, color = &quot;Model&quot;) +
  theme_party</code></pre>
